WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.465 --> 00:00:02.472
Team Polaris presents HEARTH:

2
00:00:02.472 --> 00:00:05.273
fire-safety intelligence for crewed habitats,

3
00:00:05.273 --> 00:00:10.169
built on 847 real NASA microgravity fire tests.

4
00:00:10.278 --> 00:00:11.564
On Mission overview,

5
00:00:11.564 --> 00:00:13.343
pick a habitat and see its air at a

6
00:00:13.343 --> 00:00:18.158
glance. Mini VESTA flags the hazard straight away.

7
00:00:18.006 --> 00:00:20.480
Ask VESTA in plain words.

8
00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:21.538
She flies in,

9
00:00:21.538 --> 00:00:23.425
checks the NASA data with her tools,

10
00:00:23.425 --> 00:00:24.567
cites every source,

11
00:00:24.567 --> 00:00:27.230
and tags how sure she is.

12
00:00:28.975 --> 00:00:30.081
Ask for a chart,

13
00:00:30.081 --> 00:00:32.052
and she plots every NASA test,

14
00:00:32.052 --> 00:00:33.470
oxygen against pressure,

15
00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:35.692
with your rover cabin marked.

16
00:00:35.692 --> 00:00:38.223
Not one made-up point.

17
00:00:38.079 --> 00:00:40.243
Her answers light up the matching tests on the

18
00:00:40.243 --> 00:00:42.287
habitat map.

19
00:00:42.631 --> 00:00:44.843
Test explorer filters every run,

20
00:00:44.843 --> 00:00:47.967
and VESTA can open any test for you.

21
00:00:51.075 --> 00:00:52.349
Ask her to compare,

22
00:00:52.349 --> 00:00:54.068
and she lines up ACME,

23
00:00:54.068 --> 00:00:57.395
CFI and SPICE side by side.

24
00:00:59.215 --> 00:01:01.234
Safety and gaps shows prevention,

25
00:01:01.234 --> 00:01:03.326
detection and suppression evidence,

26
00:01:03.326 --> 00:01:06.183
and what NASA has never tested.

27
00:01:06.781 --> 00:01:09.894
My data lab checks your own conditions against NASA's,

28
00:01:09.894 --> 00:01:11.925
right in your browser.

29
00:01:12.969 --> 00:01:15.962
Dataset explains every field and lets you download the

30
00:01:15.962 --> 00:01:17.777
clean data.

31
00:01:17.625 --> 00:01:20.137
The flame simulator replays real tests,

32
00:01:20.137 --> 00:01:23.057
in microgravity and on Earth.

33
00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:25.634
About tells our story.

34
00:01:25.634 --> 00:01:27.545
And if an AI service fails,

35
00:01:27.545 --> 00:01:29.023
VESTA switches engines,

36
00:01:29.023 --> 00:01:32.408
down to an offline mode that never fails.

37
00:01:32.256 --> 00:01:35.936
HEARTH. By Team Polaris.
